# .gitignore
#
# Files and folders Git should never track in this Shopify theme project.
#
# Three groups are listed below. The first is anything a tool generates on its
# own, which would otherwise change on every machine and create noise in every
# commit. The second is anything holding credentials or machine-specific paths,
# which must never reach a public repository. The third is clutter that Windows
# and macOS drop into folders without asking.
#
# Everything else in the project is theme source and should be tracked, so this
# list is deliberately short. If a file is not named here, Git will pick it up.

# Shopify CLI working directory. Holds the theme id the CLI is previewing, the
# stored storefront password, and local session state. Machine-specific and
# contains credentials, so it stays out of the repository entirely.
.shopify/

# Node dependencies, if any tooling is added later in the module. Restored from
# package.json rather than committed.
node_modules/

# Environment files. Nothing in this project needs one yet, but if one is added
# it must not be pushed.
.env
.env.local

# Log output from the CLI or any build step.
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Editor and OS clutter.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# VS Code workspace folder is tracked on purpose, because .vscode/settings.json
# is a Stretch B deliverable and should travel with the repository. Only the
# local, per-user files inside it are ignored.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
